{"title":"BITSAT","category":"Engineering","bank":"bitsat","subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","count":18,"questions":[{"id":18810,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"A parallel plate capacitor with plate area A and plate separation $d=2 \\mathrm{~m}$ has a capacitance of $4 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$.\nThe new capacitance of the system if half of the space between them is filled with a dielectric material of dielectric constant $\\mathrm{K}=3$ (as shown in figure) will be:\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252FgnNODDb46rlSYm79fYRjnQTl5L8pmrwgZaF9dr7NDfc.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FgnNODDb46rlSYm79fYRjnQTl5L8pmrwgZaF9dr7NDfc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FgnNODDb46rlSYm79fYRjnQTl5L8pmrwgZaF9dr7NDfc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>","options":["$2 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$","$32 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$","$6 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$","$8 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$"],"answer":2,"solution":"We have, $C_i=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d}=4 \\mu FC_f=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d-t+\\frac{t}{k}}=\\frac{A \\epsilon_0}{d-\\frac{d}{2}+\\frac{d}{2 \\times 3}}=\\frac{A \\in_0}{d\\left(1-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}=\\frac{4 \\mu F}{\\frac{2}{3}}=6 \\mu F$","difficulty":"Hard","source":"BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 1)","_marksId":"67726cf8c49e8ef28ee2b33b"},{"id":18811,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"A capacitor of capacitance $C$ is charged to a potential V. The flux of the electric field through a closed surface enclosing the positive plate of the capacitor is:","options":["$\\frac{C V}{2 \\varepsilon_0}$","$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{CV}}{\\varepsilon_0}$","$\\frac{\\mathrm{CV}}{\\varepsilon_0}$","<br />Zero"],"answer":2,"solution":"From the Gauss's law<br />$\\begin{aligned} \\\\ & \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\text {in }}}{\\epsilon_0}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Q}}{\\epsilon_0} \\quad \\because \\mathrm{Q}=\\mathrm{CV} \\\\ \\\\ & \\therefore \\phi=\\frac{\\mathrm{CV}}{\\epsilon_0} \\\\ \\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2023 (Memory Based Paper 2)","_marksId":"65b7b87c97ae24e9e2db8cd0"},{"id":18812,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"The work done in placing a charge of $8 \\times 10^{-18}$ coulomb on a condenser of capacity 100 microfarad is","options":["$3.1 \\times 10^{-26}$ joule","$4 \\times 10^{-10}$ joule","$32 \\times 10^{-32}$ joule","$16 \\times 10^{-32}$ joule"],"answer":2,"solution":"Work done $=\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{q}^2}{\\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{\\left(8 \\times 10^{-18}\\right)^2}{2 \\times 100 \\times 10^{-6}}$<br />$=32 \\times 10^{-32} \\mathrm{~J}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2023 (Memory Based Paper 1)","_marksId":"65b7b87097ae24e9e2db8c57"},{"id":18813,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"In a given network the equivalent capacitance between $A$ and $B$ is $C_{1}=C_{4}=1 \\mu F, C_{2}=C_{3}=2 \\mu F$.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252FUR7fH5N3eUVaBtywXMK5A3XxXEaBTe-YDzT_Imfa3NA.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FUR7fH5N3eUVaBtywXMK5A3XxXEaBTe-YDzT_Imfa3NA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FUR7fH5N3eUVaBtywXMK5A3XxXEaBTe-YDzT_Imfa3NA.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","options":["$3 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$","$6 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$","$4.5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$","$2.5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$"],"answer":0,"solution":"The equivalent circuit is shown in figure.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252FJJ0PmMzYakzoR5r60KIBHbJN9RsEesxnbhvs4TT-7M0.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FJJ0PmMzYakzoR5r60KIBHbJN9RsEesxnbhvs4TT-7M0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FJJ0PmMzYakzoR5r60KIBHbJN9RsEesxnbhvs4TT-7M0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{AB}}=1+\\frac{2 \\times 2}{2+2}+1\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{AB}}=3 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2021","_marksId":"64c0e81f6f5bfc7ab78aeaca"},{"id":18814,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"In the circuit given below, the charge in $\\mu \\mathrm{C},$ on the capacitor having $5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ is\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252FO33zcfEW8hFj-ynlLZAV1V0aMC-qTMsxK-IC-6pbWLM.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FO33zcfEW8hFj-ynlLZAV1V0aMC-qTMsxK-IC-6pbWLM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2FO33zcfEW8hFj-ynlLZAV1V0aMC-qTMsxK-IC-6pbWLM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","options":["4.5","9","7","15"],"answer":1,"solution":"Potential difference across the branch de is\r\n\r\n$6 \\mathrm{~V}$. Net capacitance of de branch is $2.1 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ So, $q=C V\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{q}=2.1 \\times 6 \\mu \\mathrm{C} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{q}=12.6 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$\r\n\r\nPotential across $3 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ capacitance is $\\mathrm{V}=\\frac{12.6}{3}=4.2 \\mathrm{volt}$\r\n\r\nPotential across 2 and 5 combination in parallel is $6-4.2=1.8 \\mathrm{~V}$\r\n\r\nSo, $q^{\\prime}=(1.8)(5)=9 \\mu C$","difficulty":"Easy","source":"BITSAT 2020","_marksId":"64c0e8116f5bfc7ab78aea50"},{"id":18815,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"<p>When a capacitor is fully charged as shown in the following figure, then current drawn from the cell is</p><p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252F9e6da9e7-b415-4494-b2d5-5afaa5c11870-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F9e6da9e7-b415-4494-b2d5-5afaa5c11870-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F9e6da9e7-b415-4494-b2d5-5afaa5c11870-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 156px;\" /></p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>When capacitor is fully charged, then it acts like a open switch, therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> resistor has no use. So, rest of the resistances <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> will be in series. Hence, current drawn from cell</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2019","_marksId":"64c0e8046f5bfc7ab78ae9d8"},{"id":18816,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"A charged capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is discharging through a resistor of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. At what time the charge on the capacitor is equal to one half of its initial value?","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo> </mo></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>The charge on the capacitor at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> in a discharging circuit is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo></math> time constant<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math>               <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>when, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Taking natural log on both side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>e</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"BITSAT 2019","_marksId":"64c0e8046f5bfc7ab78ae9d9"},{"id":18817,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"<p>A parallel plate capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> with plates of unit area and separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> is filled with a liquid of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, the level of liquid is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>initially. <img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252F974c2e8a-cf06-4938-97ce-f4fba41c1918-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F974c2e8a-cf06-4938-97ce-f4fba41c1918-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F974c2e8a-cf06-4938-97ce-f4fba41c1918-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 183px;\" /><br />Suppose, the liquid level decreases at a constant speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, the time constant as a function of time is</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>We have, the time constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Putting the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></math> in Equation. (i), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>∵</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>","difficulty":"Hard","source":"BITSAT 2018","_marksId":"64c0e7f36f5bfc7ab78ae943"},{"id":18818,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"BITSAT","q":"<p>In the given circuit diagram,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fbitsat%252F5ad9a203-a9be-4e03-bbae-704afa819346-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F5ad9a203-a9be-4e03-bbae-704afa819346-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fbitsat%2F5ad9a203-a9be-4e03-bbae-704afa819346-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Then, what will be the numerical value of charge on each plates of the capacitor.</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μC</mi></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>Current will flow only through the branch containing re